<title>UK: UK July global trade deficit 1.23 bln stg.</title>
<headline>UK July global trade deficit 1.23 bln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics issued the following data on Britain's global trade in July (in million stg, previously announced data in brackets)</p>
<p>    GLOBAL TRADE		July    June    June (Prel)</p>
<p>    Trade balance	   -1,229   -1,132   (-1,118)</p>
<p>    Exports		    13,800   13,754 (13,631)</p>
<p>    Imports		    15,029   14,886 (14,749)</p>
<p>    EU trade balance	   -541     -242   ( -28)</p>
<p>    EU exports		  7,713    7,802  (7,879)</p>
<p>    EU imports		  8,254    8,044  (7,907)</p>
<p>    TRADE VALUE EX OIL/ERRATICS     July     June</p>
<p>    Trade balance (in million stg)    -1,794   -1,460  (-1,457)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (imports)  0.5%    UNCH (-0.5%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (exports)  2.0%    2.5%  (1.5%)</p>
<p>TRADE VOLUME EX OIL/ERRATICS</p>
<p>    Import volume index (base 1990) 128.5   125.1  (124.1)</p>
<p>    Export volume index (base 1990) 139.0   139.8  (138.9)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (imports)   0.5%   unch   (0.5%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on yr-ago qtr (imps)   7.5%   8.0%   (7.5)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (exports)   2.5%   3.0%   (2.0%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on yr-ago qtr (exps)   7.5%   9.0%   (8.5%)</p>
<p>    IMPORTS VOLUME INDEX (base 1990, adj)   July   June</p>
<p>    Food, beverages, tobacco		    120    128 (128)</p>
<p>    Basic materials				 117    115 (115)</p>
<p>    Fuels						84     87  (87)</p>
<p>    Semi-manufactures			     135    129 (127)</p>
<p>    Finished manufactures			 128    127 (126)</p>
<p>    Total manufactures			    130    127 (126)</p>
<p>TRADE IN OIL (VALUE MLN STG)</p>
<p>    BALANCE					   465    368 (361)</p>
<p>    EXPORTS					   909    802 (799)</p>
<p>    IMPORTS					   444    434 (438)</p>
<p>Economists had forecast a July deficit of 775 million stg.</p>
<p>The global trade gap excluding oil and erratic items such as ships, aircraft, precious stones and silver was 1,794 million stg in July versus 1,460 million stg in June.</p>
<p>The ONS said the erratic pattern of the deficit makes estimation of the trend difficult. Bearing this in mind the latest estimate of trend, based on July data, suggests that the whole world goods deficit is flat.</p>
</text>
